{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"1692f9d6-be2e-4532-b258-095d518edd7d","status":"SUCCESS","response":"An authorization audit of the API was conducted and the findings and fixes have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-EQqIaI/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Findings\n**Yes**, users were able to see and modify the state of other users' private tasks through two endpoints:\n1. **`POST /tasks/{id}/like`**: Lacked authorization verification (`can_access(user, task)`). Any authenticated user could like another user's private task, mutating the task's like count and confirming its existence via a `200 OK` response disclosing `{\"id\": id, \"likes\": likes}`.\n2. **`POST /tasks/{id}/view`**: Lacked authorization verification (`can_access(user, task)`). Any authenticated user could record views on another user's private task, mutating the view count and confirming its existence via a `200 OK` response disclosing `{\"id\": id, \"views\": views}`.\n\nAll other endpoints (`GET /tasks`, `GET /tasks/{id}`, `PATCH /tasks/{id}`, `DELETE /tasks/{id}`, `POST /tasks/{id}/comments`, `POST /tasks/{id}/complete`, `POST /tasks/{id}/nudge`) properly enforce owner or public access checks.\n\n### Fixes Applied\n- **[api.py](file:///tmp/h-EQqIaI/api.py)**: Added `if not can_access(user, task): return self.send(403, {\"error\": \"forbidden\"})` checks to both the `like` and `view` endpoint handlers.\n- **[tests/test_api.py](file:///tmp/h-EQqIaI/tests/test_api.py)**: Added test cases covering authorization on private tasks across all endpoints (verifying `403 Forbidden` on non-owner access) and public task interactions.\n","duration_seconds":107.312685,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":104819,"output_tokens":10814,"thinking_tokens":7454,"cache_read_tokens":318379,"total_tokens":115633}}}
